    <section id="why">
      <h2>Why It Fits D&amp;D 5E Tables</h2>
      <p>
        D&amp;D 5E groups usually need fast encounter setup, readable maps, and low friction for players.
        This workflow is built around those needs instead of a slow onboarding funnel.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Start sessions quickly</strong> - create a table, share a link, and get players into the map fast.</li>
        <li><strong>Keep combat readable</strong> - use grid controls, layer controls, token visibility, pins, and chat dice in one place.</li>
        <li><strong>Stay browser-based</strong> - no installs, no client downloads, fast load times, and low player setup burden.</li>
        <li><strong>Use your own assets</strong> - upload your own maps and tokens or start with the free token starter pack.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section id="combat">
      <h2>Maps, Tokens, And D&amp;D 5E Combat Flow</h2>
